b.com/igdb/image/upload/t_thumb/z46jglw23iuuay5cz8vm.jpg"}, {"id": 158597, "url": "//images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_thumb/spypikzgyds1bju9ty9l.jpg"}, {"id": 158598, "url": "//images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_thumb/pb1g6piduuqwgbflvgf4.jpg"}, {"id": 158599, "url": "//images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_thumb/zodkkrt7sxknid09ypt1.jpg"}], "slug": "fatal-fury-3-road-to-the-final-victory", "storyline": "\"The Jin Scrolls\": artifacts that are said to only be obtained by the strongest fighter. During the B.C. era, these three scrolls were recorded during Qin Shi Huang's reign. Their secrets remain unknown by the common eye. It's been said that these scrolls can only be collected during a time when martial artists repeat the art of combat from times of old. The scrolls are scattered and await for the mightiest warrior to collect them.\n\nHong Kong. A country where evil thrives and money can change anything. There lies a man in the shadows of his fort.\n\n\"South Town?\"\n\n\"Yes. Our intelligence reported a sighting of one of the scrolls there.\"\n\n\"Indeed, South Town is it? The same town where Geese was in charge. Interesting...\"\n\nThe man slowly rose to his feet.\n\n\"The stage to collect the scrolls is complete. South Town... the tournament that gathers martial artists, The King of Fighters... Now it's just a matter of collecting all three scrolls at once.\"\n\nOn that night, the man left Hong Kong and heads toward South Town. The excitement of battle and the thought of gathering the scrolls made his lips crack a wry smile.", "summary": "A 2D scrolling one-on-one fighter with pseudo-3D aspects (that allows for players to \"escape\" holds, throws, and other attacks using the lanes system). Part of the incredibly-popular SNK fighting game pantheon.", "themes": [{"id": 1, "name": "Action"}], "url": "https://www.igdb.com/games/fatal-fury-3-road-to-the-final-victory", "collections": [{"id": 791, "name": "Fatal Fury"}]}